Summary of Hoisting Behavior
Feature	                 Hoisted?	Initialized?         Usable before Declaration?
var	                     ✅ Yes	   🚫 Undefined	        ⚠️ Allowed but undefined
let	                     ✅ Yes	   ❌ No (TDZ)	      ❌ ReferenceError
const	                 ✅ Yes	   ❌ No (TDZ)	      ❌ ReferenceError
Function Declaration	 ✅ Yes	    ✅ Fully Hoisted	  ✅ Yes
Function Expression	     ✅ Variable Hoisted	❌ No	❌ TypeError
Class Declaration	     ✅ Yes	❌ No (TDZ)	❌ ReferenceError


🔹 Best Practices to Avoid Hoisting Issues
✅ Declare variables and functions at the beginning of their scope.
✅ Use let and const instead of var to avoid accidental undefined values.
✅ Use function declarations if you need to call a function before defining it.
✅ Avoid using classes before declaration to prevent errors.